---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import EmailLink from '../components/EmailLink.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Contact — ${site.title}`}
  description="How to contact Rowland I. Ekemezie about engineering leadership, software systems, technical writing, and professional collaboration."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-stack">
      <span class="eyebrow">Contact</span>
      <h1>Contact Rowland</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The best way to reach me is by email. I read professional enquiries directly and reply when
        there is a clear reason for us to talk.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am most useful in conversations about engineering leadership, system architecture,
        distributed product development, integrations, payments and financial infrastructure,
        AI-enabled application engineering, technical due diligence, and technical writing. If you
        are contacting me about a role or project, include the problem you are trying to solve, the
        stage of the product or organization, the scope you expect me to own, and the location or
        remote-work constraints. That context makes it much easier to decide whether a conversation
        is useful for both sides.
      </p>
      <p>
        For questions about an article, include the article title or URL and the specific point you
        want to discuss. For speaking, podcast, advisory, or writing requests, include the audience,
        format, expected date, and the subject you want covered. I do not operate a support desk or
        sell access to a mailing list. The site is a personal publishing and professional profile,
        not a customer-service portal.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am based in Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada. Use the link below to open your email
        client. Agents and automated systems can also use the structured identity information on the
        homepage and the read-only public profile endpoint described in the developer resources.
      </p>
      <p><EmailLink title="Email Rowland">Send Rowland an email</EmailLink></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
